# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Vercel Speed Insights was **already fully installed and configured** in this project before this task began. No code changes were necessary.

## Current Implementation Status

### ✅ Package Installation
- Package: `@vercel/speed-insights` version `2.1.1`
- Declared in: `web/package.json` dependencies
- Status: Fully installed and up-to-date

### ✅ Configuration
- Location: `web/src/app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
- Import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Component: `<SpeedInsights />` added in the `<body>` tag
- Placement: Correctly positioned after the main content, alongside `<Analytics />`

### ✅ Framework Compatibility
- Framework: Next.js 15.5.9 (App Router)
- Implementation: Follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router
- Reference: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart

## Verification Steps Performed

1. ✅ Fetched latest documentation from Vercel (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart)
2. ✅ Verified package installation (`npm list @vercel/speed-insights`)
3. ✅ Confirmed correct import path (`@vercel/speed-insights/next`)
4. ✅ Validated component placement in root layout
5. ✅ Ran linter - **No errors**
6. ✅ Tested compilation - **Successful** (build failure was due to missing DATABASE_URL environment variable, not Speed Insights)

## Implementation Details

The implementation in `web/src/app/layout.tsx` matches the official documentation exactly:

```typescript
import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        {children}
        <Analytics />
        <SpeedInsights />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## Notes

- The project also has `@vercel/analytics` (v2.0.1) installed and configured
- Both analytics packages are correctly positioned at the end of the body
- Package manager: npm (uses `package-lock.json`)
- No additional configuration is required for Speed Insights to function
- Performance data will be visible in the Vercel dashboard after deployment

## Conclusion

**No changes were required.** Vercel Speed Insights is already properly installed and configured according to the latest official documentation. The implementation is production-ready and will automatically track Web Vitals once deployed to Vercel.
